		<h2>Unsourced figures</h2>
		<p>
			The talk twice puts current Massachusetts emissions at roughly 60 million metric tons a year,
			on the carbon budget slide and again on the forests as climate infrastructure slide. The
			supporting documentation does not name a source for it.
		</p>
		<p>
			The land-use slide carries two more. The August 10 version puts the out-of-state forest
			behind Massachusetts wood consumption at 573,000 acres, up from the 45,000 acres the August
			6 version gave, and the out-of-state crop and grazing land behind about 90 percent of the
			state's food at 6.4 million acres, down from 17 million acres for more than 85 percent. John
			attributes the forest figure to published in-state harvesting rates per harvested acre. He
			names no source for either number, and the supporting documentation predates the change.
		</p>
		<p>
			All three are context rather than inputs. None of the results above depend on them.
		</p>
